_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02854355698200909,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":42.8,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.024832998989894935,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":58.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.18464,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"TKO Group Holdings, Inc. operates as a sports and entertainment company. The company operates through three segments: UFC, WWE and IMG. The UFC segment distributes programming content; ticket sales and site fees associated with the business's global live events; partnerships and marketing; and consumer products licensing agreements of UFC-branded products. The WWE segment consists of media rights fees associated with the distribution of its programming content; ticket sales and site fees associated with the business's global live events; partnerships and marketing; and consumer products licensing agreements of WWE-branded products. The IMG segment specializing in media rights management and sales, multi-channel content production and distribution, brand partnerships, strategic consulting, digital services, and event management. This segment also offers hospitality business, offering ticketing, curated guest experiences, live event production and travel management services. It is also involved in the merchandising of video games, apparel, equipment, trading cards, memorabilia, digital goods, and toys. In addition, the company engages in the sponsorships and advertising business, which offers sale of in-venue and in-broadcast advertising assets, content product integration, and digital impressions. The company was incorporated in 2023 and is based in New York, New York. TKO Group Holdings, Inc. is a subsidiary of WME Group, Inc.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ariel Zev Emanuel | Executive Chair & CEO | Age 65 | Compensation: $23.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the top quartile among Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 68%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $29K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 20\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["TKO Group Holdings, Inc. is a large-cap communication services business with a $36.9B market cap on $4.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +68% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 18% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 506% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":5.056719630460592},{"text":"Goodwill represents 54% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.7% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $23.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014 legacy distribution bundles unravel faster than subscription revenue can replace them.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 9% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Growing faster than most Communication Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Raised Revenue Guidance Will Impact TKO Group Holdings Stock","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/media/nyse-tko/tko-group-holdings/news/how-raised-revenue-guidance-will-impact-tko-group-holdings-s","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794616899.136,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.84,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Massachusetts Financial Services Reports 5.23% Stake in TKO Group Holdings Inc","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/massachusetts-financial-services-reports-523-stake-in-tko-group-holdings-inc","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794588866.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Investment Analysts\u2019 Wee